.TH VFORK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
vfork \- create a child sharing the parent's address space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B pid_t vfork(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a child while suspending the calling parent thread until the child
executes a new program or exits. The child shares the parent's address space
and stack. The child must immediately call execve or _exit, must not return
from the calling function, modify data, or invoke other library functions.
Other threads, if present, are not suspended.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero in the child, the child PID in the parent, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (3crunch),
.BR execve (3crunch),
.BR vfork (2)
